   },
   {
    "frase": "different crystalline arrangements of the compound itself leading  to polymorphs, which differ either by the conformation of the  molecule, by the overall packing, or by a combination of both.[2] In  addition, solvent mo",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2",
     "3",
     "4"
    ],
    "n": 3
   },
   {
    "frase": "Polymorphism in pharmaceutical materials is widely  studied,[5] and normally every newly developed drug compound is  subjected to extensive crystal form screening[5c] in order to  discover as many of the experimentally a",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "5",
     "6"
    ],
    "n": 2
   },
   {
    "frase": "However, this approach is money- and time-consuming and  it does not guarantee the isolation of all possible stable crystal  forms, as cases such as that of Ritonavir show.[7] Thus, a more  fundamental understanding of t",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "7"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "DOI: 10.1002/chem.201xxxxxx",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "10.1002"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "polymorphic and solvated crystal forms is an ongoing key  objective.[5a, 8]",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "8"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "In particular the interplay of the mutual interactions of  the functional groups on the drug molecules themselves and their  interactions with solvent molecules during crystallisation from  solution or the melt is rarely",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "9",
     "10"
    ],
    "n": 2
   },
   {
    "frase": "Two directional intermolecular interactions play a key role  during crystallisation and in the crystalline state, namely hydrogen  bonding and halogen bonding.[11] Hydrogen bonding has been  found to stabilise crystal st",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "11",
     "12",
     "13",
     "14",
     "15"
    ],
    "n": 5
   },
   {
    "frase": "In addition to hydrogen bonding, halogen bonds are  increasingly recognised as a key directional interaction in  molecular crystal structures.[16] Even though these interactions  are generally considerably weaker than hy",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "16",
     "17",
     "18",
     "19"
    ],
    "n": 4
   },
   {
    "frase": "In this study, we seek to understand the interplay of  hydrogen and halogen bonding and their influence on the crystal  forms of an X-ray contrast molecule, diatrizoic acid (DTA,  Scheme 1), which is pharmaceutically rel",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "20",
     "21"
    ],
    "n": 2
   },
   {
    "frase": "Specifically monographed crystal forms are  generally prevalent and stable enough for manufacture, and since  DTA is poorly water soluble, the formation of a hydrate indicates  severe problems for pharmaceutical manufact",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "22"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Another new  application of the contrast molecule is its immobilisation on the  surface of gold nanoparticles for IV administration as contrast for  enhanced computed tomography.[24]",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "24"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Folen et al. have reported the dihydrate form of DTA as  well as an additional anhydrous modification, which in this study  will be referred to as form I.[25] We have previously reported three  dimethylsulfoxide solvates",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "25",
     "26",
     "27"
    ],
    "n": 3
   },
   {
    "frase": "Results The crystal forms  Diatrizoic acid was found to exist in two hydrated forms: the  known dihydrate[25] and a new form which contains one water  molecule per four host molecules (a tetarto hydrate).",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "25"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "DOI: 10.1002/chem.201xxxxxx",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "10.1002"
    ],
    "n": 1
