    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "The monosodium salt of diatrizoic acid has been previously  reported by Tonnessen et al.[23] and shows a higher solubility in  water than DTA and can be crystallised by precipitation from  aqueous solution with anti-solv",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "23"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Surprisingly, the dehydration does not take place at very high  temperatures, as would be expected for the strongly coordinating  hydrates of organic sodium salts.[34] Upon further heating, melting  occurs at 278 °C.",
